WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.700
 Let's do this.

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:02.402
 Keep everyone alive.

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:07.207
 Holy geez.

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:10.143
 Hiya!

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.016
 The nine ring broadsword.

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:20.319
NARRATOR: The nine
ring broadsword

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:22.855
is a variant on the Chinese
dao from the Qing dynasty

00:00:22.921 --> 00:00:24.624
that was used through the 1930s.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.226
Featuring a blade wider than
a traditional dao and a curve

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:30.129
towards the tip, the weapon
was ideal for chopping

00:00:30.195 --> 00:00:32.965
and could sever a head
with a single swing.

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:34.267
The rings on the
back of the blade

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.836
serve dual purposes,
for ornamentation used

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:39.439
during ceremonies or
martial arts displays

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:41.407
and for superstitious
reasons, as it

00:00:41.473 --> 00:00:44.511
was believed that jingling sound
would ward off evil spirits.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:47.680
This deadly and sacred sword
can be seen on the television

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:50.817
show "Into the Badlands."

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:55.155
 Bladesmiths, you
have our gratitude.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:02.929
Gentlemen, your swords
look magnificent,

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:05.531
but are they deadly?

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:07.367
To find that out, we
will take your swords

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:11.170
and deliver some clean
blows on this pig carcass.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:14.006
It's all about the kill
in this particular test.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.176
Britain, you are first.

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:17.010
Are you ready, sir?

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.378
 Yes, sir.

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:19.446
 Let's do this.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:55.782
 Well, there it went.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:07.093
 All right, Britain, first up.

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:11.664
What I love about this
blade was the balance,

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:16.068
the way I was able to move
with the blade everywhere.

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.070
Now let's talk
about the breakage.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:20.939
OK, so the break
happened right there

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:22.775
where the ring was attached.

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:26.045
You can see it's really not a
bad [inaudible] you have there.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:29.048
It could be finer, but rings,
when you're digging into that,

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.984
could cause stress risers.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.553
And it broke right there
where the ring was.

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:40.126
Well gentlemen, the fight
is not over, because Mike,

00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:43.596
your blade still has
to survive nine strikes

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.598
on its kill test target.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:46.832
Good luck, gentlemen.

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:48.367
Doug.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.369
 If I make it through
nine strikes on this pig,

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.104
I'm Forged in Fire champion.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:53.339
My palms are sweating.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:54.340
I'm so scared that
this thing is going

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.575
to break on the first swing.

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:41.621
 Good job, Bro.

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:51.230
 Burton, unfortunately
your blade broke.

00:03:51.296 --> 00:03:53.565
It can no longer
continue with testing.

00:03:53.632 --> 00:03:57.403
And for that reason, I have
dismiss you from the forge.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.038
You did a good job, brother.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:00.005
 I appreciate that.

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:00.974
 It sucks.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:01.773
 Gorgeous weapon.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.209
 Thank you, man.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:05.144
Seeing my blade break,
it's a disappointment.

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.880
You know, when you make it to
round three, you want to win.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.716
You know, the nine holes
burnt through four drill bits

00:04:10.816 --> 00:04:12.751
doing them, so
somewhere through there

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:14.720
I probably was giving a
little too much pressure

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.990
and caused the stress riser
to run down that blade.

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:21.360
That was enough to cause a
critical failure in that blade.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.562
I'm still proud of myself
with what I've done, you know.

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:26.164
It was a way out
of my wheelhouse.

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:28.268
What's next for
me is not swords,

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:31.537
especially any nine ring
swords, that's for damn sure.

00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:35.675
 Mike, congratulations.

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:37.609
The strength and
integrity of your blade

00:04:37.709 --> 00:04:40.012
has made you a Forged
in Fire champion

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:43.049
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:04:43.115 --> 00:04:46.118
Good job, brother.

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:47.686
 I won Forged in Fire.

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:48.854
Holy crap, man.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:50.523
 Come on forward and
shake our hands, my friend.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:51.356
 Thank you.

00:04:51.423 --> 00:04:52.691
- Good job.
- Thank you.

00:04:52.758 --> 00:04:54.193
Some of the things that
went wrong in my home

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.795
forge, I was really
sure that that blade

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:56.828
was going to break on me.

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:57.697
But it didn't.

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:02.568
This is a happy dance.

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:03.436
Do it all day.

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:14.981
 The Tuareg takouba.

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:21.587
The takouba is a
type of broadsword

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:24.323
that has been used by the
nomadic Tuareg people of North

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:26.726
Africa since the 14th century.

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:28.227
This double-edged
lightweight blade

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:30.563
was carried for self-defense
on long journeys,

00:05:30.629 --> 00:05:33.265
designed to deliver
lethal slashes and stabs

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:35.501
against a rival warrior.

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.069
Due to the Tuareg's
aversion to iron,

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:40.372
there is no exposed steel or
iron on the hilt of the sword,

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.541
so it cannot touch
the user's hand.

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:43.943
Measuring more
than a meter long,

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:46.112
this deadly weapon was
seen as a symbol of wealth.

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:49.749
Some members of the Takouba clan
still carry this weapon today.

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:55.721
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:58.424
Your Taureg takoubas
look beautiful,

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:01.494
but the kind of beauty I'm
looking for is the lethal kind.

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:03.830
I'm going to take your weapon,
deliver some lethal blows

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.431
to this ballistics dummy.

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:06.198
Dustin, you're first.

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:06.999
Ready?

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:07.766
 Yes, sir.

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:09.902
 Let's do this.

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:13.506
[rock music playing]

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:35.461
[laughing]

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:36.561
 All right, Dustin.

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:38.630
Let's talk about
your weapon here.

00:06:38.697 --> 00:06:42.167
First up, your
handle construction.

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:44.270
I like the ovoid feel of this.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.172
The flare you have
there in your pummel

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:48.674
actually gives great
retention for this.

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:51.743
Your tip is sharp
enough to penetrate,

00:06:51.843 --> 00:06:54.113
your edges are sharp
when you're cutting out,

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:57.616
and you can wield this
to do that kind of damage

00:06:57.683 --> 00:06:59.418
on this ballistic dummy.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:03.922
Overall, sir, a weapon
like this, it will kill.

00:07:03.989 --> 00:07:05.290
 Awesome.

00:07:05.357 --> 00:07:06.325
 All right, Joshua.
Your turn.

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:07.259
You ready?

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:08.160
 Keep everyone alive.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.562
 All right, let's do this.

00:07:12.899 --> 00:07:16.502
[rock music playing]

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:39.658
 All right.

00:07:39.725 --> 00:07:41.193
Joshua, let's talk
about your weapon here.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.729
Your pummel right here could
have used some weight to it,

00:07:43.796 --> 00:07:46.098
but because it's forward
weighted and the fact

00:07:46.164 --> 00:07:49.801
that you have a very sharp edge,
every slice that you can see

00:07:49.868 --> 00:07:51.970
is very deep into
the ballistics dummy.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:56.775
And more importantly, sir,
your weapon, it will kill.

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:57.677
 Yeah.

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:05.284
 All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test.

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:07.686
Our desert well chop.

00:08:07.753 --> 00:08:10.689
Now, to test the strength
and overall construction

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:13.392
of your blades, I will
be chopping into our well

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:15.427
house as well as the well.

00:08:15.527 --> 00:08:16.762
Dustin, you're on deck.

00:08:16.862 --> 00:08:17.763
You ready?

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.265
 I guess so.

00:08:19.365 --> 00:08:21.200
 OK.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:24.871
[rock music playing]

00:08:55.133 --> 00:08:56.369
 All right.

00:08:56.435 --> 00:08:58.737
We were doing so well
for a moment there.

00:08:58.837 --> 00:09:04.476
What actually happened was,
with insetting your blade down

00:09:04.576 --> 00:09:07.946
into this piece of wood,
any of that leverage

00:09:08.013 --> 00:09:11.917
was just too much for the wood
itself and it popped it loose.

00:09:12.017 --> 00:09:15.154
Your tang is a little bit
small, but what I do like to see

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:18.724
is that your blade actually
held up beautifully.

00:09:18.824 --> 00:09:20.759
I mean, your grain
structure looks fine.

00:09:20.859 --> 00:09:23.362
This is an absolutely
brutal test.

00:09:23.429 --> 00:09:24.196
Very well done.

00:09:24.263 --> 00:09:25.031
 Thank you.

00:09:29.068 --> 00:09:31.670
Now, Dustin, you survived
every one of the strikes

00:09:31.737 --> 00:09:33.038
except for the last one.

00:09:33.138 --> 00:09:35.941
Your guard gave way and
your blade followed.

00:09:36.008 --> 00:09:37.542
So we consider this a
catastrophic failure.

00:09:37.609 --> 00:09:39.312
Cannot continue
testing your blade.

00:09:39.378 --> 00:09:41.213
But you're not out
of the fight yet.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.514
How are you feeling, Joshua?

00:09:42.615 --> 00:09:43.348
 Pressure's on.

00:09:43.448 --> 00:09:44.816
 All right.

00:09:44.883 --> 00:09:46.485
So you need to survive
five strikes in order to be

00:09:46.585 --> 00:09:48.520
named Forged in Fire champion.

00:09:48.621 --> 00:09:49.488
Are you ready?

00:09:49.555 --> 00:09:50.222
 Yes, sir.

00:09:50.289 --> 00:09:50.989
 All right.

00:09:51.056 --> 00:09:53.392
Let's do it.

00:09:53.459 --> 00:09:57.096
[rock music playing]

00:10:14.513 --> 00:10:16.715
 Well, Joshua, your
blade is strong.

00:10:16.781 --> 00:10:18.416
It made it past all the strikes.

00:10:18.517 --> 00:10:20.018
Congratulations.

00:10:20.085 --> 00:10:22.621
Now Dustin, unfortunately for
you that means your time here

00:10:22.688 --> 00:10:24.389
in this competition has
ended because you did

00:10:24.489 --> 00:10:25.791
have a catastrophic failure.

00:10:25.858 --> 00:10:27.493
It was an honor watching
you in our forge,

00:10:27.559 --> 00:10:28.660
but unfortunately,
man, at this time

00:10:28.727 --> 00:10:30.129
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:10:30.196 --> 00:10:32.064
step off our forge floor.

00:10:32.131 --> 00:10:32.732
 Thank you guys.

00:10:32.832 --> 00:10:34.066
 Thank you so much.

00:10:34.133 --> 00:10:35.100
 I'm definitely crushed.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.802
I actually thought that
recessing the sword

00:10:37.903 --> 00:10:40.005
into the tang a little bit
would make it stronger,

00:10:40.072 --> 00:10:42.207
and that's kind of what
bit me in the end, so

00:10:42.274 --> 00:10:44.710
definitely definitely
won't be doing that again.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:46.712
I'm definitely
proud of this blade.

00:10:46.779 --> 00:10:48.747
I came here to challenge
myself as much as I could

00:10:48.813 --> 00:10:51.016
and I definitely achieved that.

00:10:51.083 --> 00:10:53.052
 Well Joshua,
congratulations man.

00:10:53.118 --> 00:10:54.887
That means you are the newest
Forged in Fire champion.

00:10:54.953 --> 00:10:58.057
You just got yourself
a check for $10,000.

00:10:58.124 --> 00:11:01.059
Congratulations.

00:11:01.159 --> 00:11:02.594
 Yeah!

00:11:02.661 --> 00:11:03.996
Oh my gosh.

00:11:04.063 --> 00:11:06.331
I made a sword
that didn't break.

00:11:06.398 --> 00:11:07.900
Oh my gosh.

00:11:07.967 --> 00:11:12.905
It was a hard competition,
so this is unreal.

00:11:13.005 --> 00:11:13.739
Oh.

00:11:24.449 --> 00:11:25.918
 The Polish karabela.

00:11:28.253 --> 00:11:30.088
NARRATOR: One of Europe's
most iconic sabers,

00:11:30.155 --> 00:11:32.591
the karabela was a side
arm of history's most

00:11:32.658 --> 00:11:35.060
fearsome cavalry,
the Winget hussars.

00:11:35.126 --> 00:11:37.963
These 17th century warriors
famed for their feathered armor

00:11:38.029 --> 00:11:39.898
and sophisticated
attack formations,

00:11:39.965 --> 00:11:41.533
brandished the
sword on horseback

00:11:41.599 --> 00:11:42.968
when closing in on the enemy.

00:11:43.035 --> 00:11:44.903
The saber's light
curved blade slashed

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.738
easily through enemy armor.

00:11:46.838 --> 00:11:48.474
Its hilt often
included fixtures that

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:52.244
improved grip and recovery,
like a thumb ring, chain guard,

00:11:52.311 --> 00:11:54.079
or curved eagle head pummel.

00:11:54.146 --> 00:11:56.915
The karabela was so effective
at helping the hussars defeat

00:11:56.982 --> 00:11:59.017
enemy armies much
larger in size,

00:11:59.118 --> 00:12:01.120
that it became a
symbol of prestige

00:12:01.186 --> 00:12:05.023
worn by Polish Lithuanian
nobility at formal events.

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:09.995
Its legacy lives on in the
video game series "Witcher."

00:12:10.061 --> 00:12:12.531
 Bladesmiths, this
is the kill test.

00:12:12.598 --> 00:12:15.667
To see what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:12:15.767 --> 00:12:17.502
I will take your weapon,
deliver some slashes

00:12:17.602 --> 00:12:20.805
and thrusts on this pig carcass.

00:12:20.872 --> 00:12:21.640
Ethan, you're up first.

00:12:21.707 --> 00:12:22.408
You ready?

00:12:22.475 --> 00:12:25.578
 I am so ready.

00:12:25.678 --> 00:12:29.215
[rock music playing]

00:12:39.458 --> 00:12:41.360
 All right How'd it feel?

00:12:44.296 --> 00:12:46.665
 First up, there are
no issues whatsoever

00:12:46.732 --> 00:12:47.532
with your edge over here.

00:12:47.632 --> 00:12:48.600
It is sharp.

00:12:48.666 --> 00:12:50.802
It lacerates and cuts cleanly.

00:12:50.902 --> 00:12:53.172
Look at that razor
cuts right there.

00:12:53.238 --> 00:12:54.973
On the thrust you
have an angle here

00:12:55.073 --> 00:12:57.309
that allowed for a deep
thrust, pulling out

00:12:57.376 --> 00:12:58.810
and slashing on the way out.

00:12:58.910 --> 00:13:03.548
Overall your weapon will kill.

00:13:03.615 --> 00:13:04.316
All right.

00:13:04.383 --> 00:13:05.284
Liam, your turn.

00:13:05.351 --> 00:13:06.051
You ready?
- Oh, yeah.

00:13:06.118 --> 00:13:06.851
Let's do it.

00:13:06.918 --> 00:13:08.420
So many things can go wrong.

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:11.456
I don't even know if I was
able to get a good solid temper

00:13:11.557 --> 00:13:13.192
on this blade.

00:13:13.259 --> 00:13:16.862
[rock music playing]

00:13:36.981 --> 00:13:38.383
 Well, Liam, let me say this.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:41.887
First up, your presence
here is a victory.

00:13:41.987 --> 00:13:43.355
All the things that
you went through

00:13:43.422 --> 00:13:46.525
and you still turn in a
blade that's beautiful

00:13:46.592 --> 00:13:49.228
in craftsmanship
that is very sharp.

00:13:49.294 --> 00:13:52.197
But your blade did
break and you can

00:13:52.297 --> 00:13:53.932
see right here in the
cross section there's

00:13:53.998 --> 00:13:55.300
just a discoloration down here.

00:13:55.400 --> 00:13:57.902
So something happened in
your heat treating process.

00:13:57.969 --> 00:14:01.173
It may have micro fractures.

00:14:01.273 --> 00:14:02.241
It is what it is.

00:14:10.782 --> 00:14:13.018
 Liam, there was a
flaw in your blade

00:14:13.085 --> 00:14:15.053
that led to a
catastrophic blade failure

00:14:15.153 --> 00:14:17.089
and we can no longer
continue with testing.

00:14:17.189 --> 00:14:21.393
For that reason, I have to ask
you to please leave the forge.

00:14:21.493 --> 00:14:23.361
 Thank you gentlemen.

00:14:23.428 --> 00:14:24.864
I'm upset.

00:14:24.964 --> 00:14:27.999
Sometimes the best you can
do isn't going to be enough,

00:14:28.066 --> 00:14:30.336
but that doesn't mean,
you shouldn't still try.

00:14:32.671 --> 00:14:35.273
 Ethan, this is a competition
where the best player wins

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:37.976
and you, sir, are new
Forged in Fire champion,

00:14:38.076 --> 00:14:40.679
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:14:40.779 --> 00:14:42.848
Good job.

00:14:42.948 --> 00:14:45.284
 I really would have liked
to have seen both of those

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:48.120
go all the way through
testing, but I'm

00:14:48.186 --> 00:14:50.054
very proud of the work I did.

00:14:50.154 --> 00:14:52.524
And now Forged in Fire champion.

00:14:52.591 --> 00:14:55.628
[howling]

00:15:04.637 --> 00:15:07.106
 Attila the Hun's
Sword of Mars.

00:15:10.142 --> 00:15:11.076
 Yes.

00:15:11.143 --> 00:15:12.244
NARRATOR: Known as
the Scourge of God,

00:15:12.311 --> 00:15:13.778
Attila the Hun was
one of the most

00:15:13.878 --> 00:15:15.513
feared conquerors in history.

00:15:15.613 --> 00:15:18.617
The leader of the Hunnic Empire,
his group of nomadic tribes

00:15:18.684 --> 00:15:21.386
wreaked havoc across Europe
during the fifth century.

00:15:21.453 --> 00:15:23.522
Though he was once a
great ally to them,

00:15:23.622 --> 00:15:26.458
he plauged Roman territories,
sacking major cities

00:15:26.525 --> 00:15:27.927
like Constantinople.

00:15:28.027 --> 00:15:30.062
Legend states that Attila
was given the Sword of Mars

00:15:30.129 --> 00:15:32.965
by a herdsman, fulfilling a
prophecy and a direct sign

00:15:33.032 --> 00:15:36.201
from the Roman war god,
Mars, of his divine rule.

00:15:36.268 --> 00:15:38.303
The lethal weapon featured
a curved handle with a spear

00:15:38.369 --> 00:15:40.906
point tip that gave it
exceptional control,

00:15:40.972 --> 00:15:43.008
allowing for accurate
and brutal thrusts.

00:15:43.075 --> 00:15:45.276
After Attila's death
in the year 453,

00:15:45.376 --> 00:15:47.312
the Hunnic Empire
quickly dissolved.

00:15:47.379 --> 00:15:49.448
However, the story of
Attila's many conquests

00:15:49.548 --> 00:15:52.517
still live on through the
television miniseries "Attila."

00:15:52.584 --> 00:15:54.153
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:15:54.219 --> 00:15:56.355
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:15:56.422 --> 00:15:59.291
I will deliver killing blows
on this ballistics dummy.

00:15:59.358 --> 00:16:00.759
Randy, you're up first.
You ready?

00:16:00.859 --> 00:16:01.493
 I am.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:02.361
 Let's do this.

00:16:05.164 --> 00:16:08.300
[rock music playing]

00:16:27.419 --> 00:16:28.586
 All right.

00:16:28.653 --> 00:16:30.321
[inaudible] let's talk about
your Sword of Mars here.

00:16:30.388 --> 00:16:33.358
First up, the Damascus pattern
you have here is gorgeous.

00:16:33.458 --> 00:16:34.559
 Thank you.

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.794
 The weapon design is very
aggressive for thrusting

00:16:36.895 --> 00:16:38.096
and slashing.

00:16:38.162 --> 00:16:39.498
Now, your handle construction.

00:16:39.564 --> 00:16:42.667
If you reverse this,
it'll be easier to have

00:16:42.767 --> 00:16:44.169
something to lock on to.

00:16:44.236 --> 00:16:45.770
The fact that the
flare is right here,

00:16:45.837 --> 00:16:49.207
forcing my hand to open up if
I want to marry into the hilt.

00:16:49.274 --> 00:16:50.776
This is a very sharp weapon.

00:16:50.842 --> 00:16:55.046
The tip pierces all the way
through, cuts on the way out.

00:16:55.113 --> 00:16:58.683
It's pointy and scary
and it will kill.

00:16:58.750 --> 00:16:59.517
 Thank you.

00:16:59.584 --> 00:17:00.285
 Good job.

00:17:00.386 --> 00:17:01.119
All right, Dan.

00:17:01.219 --> 00:17:02.186
It is your turn.
Are you ready?

00:17:02.286 --> 00:17:03.522
 Hell yeah.
Let's do this.

00:17:03.622 --> 00:17:04.823
I was hoping the kill
test would be a dummy.

00:17:04.923 --> 00:17:08.827
I know heads will roll.

00:17:08.894 --> 00:17:12.431
[rock music playing]

00:17:30.816 --> 00:17:31.816
 All right, Dan.

00:17:31.917 --> 00:17:32.950
Let's talk about
your weapon here.

00:17:33.051 --> 00:17:34.419
I love the balance
of your blade.

00:17:34.486 --> 00:17:38.056
When I go forward, it's
not hard to pull back to go

00:17:38.156 --> 00:17:39.291
in again for another kill.

00:17:39.357 --> 00:17:40.926
Now your handle construction.

00:17:41.026 --> 00:17:42.961
It's curved enough
to where it doesn't

00:17:43.028 --> 00:17:44.262
want to fly out of my hand.

00:17:44.362 --> 00:17:46.031
It's got a good grip
and control for this.

00:17:46.131 --> 00:17:49.567
Your edge allows for very
deep cuts into the abdomen

00:17:49.667 --> 00:17:51.136
right there.

00:17:51.203 --> 00:17:53.972
The only issue we have is
that your tip picked up a bend

00:17:54.072 --> 00:17:55.974
when it chopped into the spine.

00:17:56.074 --> 00:17:58.710
But your weapon, sir, will kill.

00:17:58.810 --> 00:17:59.611
 Thank you.

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:04.516
 All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test.

00:18:04.583 --> 00:18:07.886
Now, Attila's armies were
basically one large cavalry,

00:18:07.953 --> 00:18:09.420
and through his
military campaigns

00:18:09.487 --> 00:18:12.357
he revolutionized the use of
horse in military conflicts.

00:18:12.457 --> 00:18:14.593
So to test the strength and
durability of your blades,

00:18:14.659 --> 00:18:17.896
I'll be chopping into
these horse skulls.

00:18:17.996 --> 00:18:18.797
 Randy, you're up first.

00:18:18.864 --> 00:18:19.597
Are you ready?

00:18:19.697 --> 00:18:22.767
 I guess so.

00:18:22.834 --> 00:18:26.438
[rock music playing]

00:18:39.184 --> 00:18:42.353
 OK, so right off the
bat the biggest thing

00:18:42.453 --> 00:18:47.493
is that this section, from
right about here to here,

00:18:47.559 --> 00:18:49.293
has lost its edge.

00:18:49.393 --> 00:18:53.798
There's a couple of small roles.

00:18:53.898 --> 00:18:55.066
Blade's still straight.

00:18:55.133 --> 00:18:55.933
It's all in one piece.

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:56.768
Still solid.

00:18:56.835 --> 00:18:57.736
Nicely done.

00:18:57.836 --> 00:18:58.670
It's a very strong blade.

00:18:58.737 --> 00:18:59.605
- Thank you.
- All right.

00:18:59.705 --> 00:19:00.672
Dan, are you ready?

00:19:00.772 --> 00:19:02.574
 No, but let's do it.

00:19:02.641 --> 00:19:03.609
 Everybody says that.

00:19:07.379 --> 00:19:10.549
[rock music playing]

00:19:23.895 --> 00:19:30.035
 [inaudible]

00:19:30.135 --> 00:19:32.971
 OK, so before we
get to the obvious,

00:19:33.038 --> 00:19:35.273
I really like the
design of your blade.

00:19:35.339 --> 00:19:36.941
It's got a great weight to it.

00:19:37.042 --> 00:19:38.343
Had a really good
feel in my hand.

00:19:38.443 --> 00:19:40.511
The balance was really nice.

00:19:40.611 --> 00:19:43.682
See all that space
around your tang?

00:19:43.782 --> 00:19:47.385
With that room for that blade
to move inside the guard,

00:19:47.485 --> 00:19:51.189
it could just create so much
stress that it cut loose

00:19:51.289 --> 00:19:52.657
right there at the corner.

00:19:52.757 --> 00:19:55.226
If it were all tight, there
wouldn't be any stress.

00:19:55.327 --> 00:19:56.561
There's no
discoloration here so,

00:19:56.627 --> 00:19:59.030
it's not that there was
a crack here before.

00:19:59.096 --> 00:20:00.465
The grain structure looks fine.

00:20:00.532 --> 00:20:02.801
It was a well designed
piece, but obvious flaw.

00:20:05.904 --> 00:20:08.874
 Dan, unfortunately your blade
suffered a catastrophic failure

00:20:08.941 --> 00:20:10.541
in the middle of
our strength test,

00:20:10.641 --> 00:20:13.411
which means that we
can no longer test it.

00:20:13.511 --> 00:20:15.480
I'd like to invite you
to shake our hands,

00:20:15.546 --> 00:20:17.782
shake your competitor's
hand, and then

00:20:17.849 --> 00:20:19.484
please leave the forge.

00:20:19.584 --> 00:20:21.887
 It hurts, but my
sword breaking, it's

00:20:21.987 --> 00:20:23.054
going to be a
reminder that I have

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:24.689
to push harder and be better.

00:20:24.756 --> 00:20:28.026
 Randy, the strength and
efficiency of your weapon

00:20:28.126 --> 00:20:29.494
in the kill test have
earned you the title

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:32.997
of Forged in Fire champion
and a check for how much?

00:20:33.064 --> 00:20:33.931
 $10,000.

00:20:33.998 --> 00:20:35.099
 That's right. $10,000.

00:20:35.199 --> 00:20:36.200
Good job, brother.

00:20:36.267 --> 00:20:37.502
 I won Forged in Fire.

00:20:37.603 --> 00:20:38.837
That's reality.

00:20:38.903 --> 00:20:39.537
 How do you feel?

00:20:39.604 --> 00:20:40.872
 Good.

00:20:40.972 --> 00:20:44.041
To be a champion and be
recognized as a good bladesmith

00:20:44.142 --> 00:20:46.044
is real good.

00:20:46.111 --> 00:20:48.914
This is my happy
and excited face.

00:20:48.981 --> 00:20:49.614
 Well done, sir.

00:20:49.714 --> 00:20:50.448
 Thank you.

00:20:50.515 --> 00:20:51.783
 If you didn't recognize it.

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:04.028
 The sodegarami.

00:21:04.128 --> 00:21:06.198
 Holy geez.

00:21:06.298 --> 00:21:07.632
Oh my god.

00:21:07.732 --> 00:21:09.734
NARRATOR: One of the most
intimidating and versatile

00:21:09.834 --> 00:21:12.170
Japanese pole weapons,
the sodegarami

00:21:12.237 --> 00:21:14.472
was part of the key
arsenal for samurai police

00:21:14.539 --> 00:21:16.307
during the 17th century.

00:21:16.408 --> 00:21:18.476
Featuring lethal
spikes and hooks,

00:21:18.576 --> 00:21:21.045
police were able to
capture violent offenders

00:21:21.146 --> 00:21:22.613
from a distance by
using the weapon

00:21:22.713 --> 00:21:26.618
to latch onto the suspects,
stopping them in their tracks.

00:21:26.685 --> 00:21:28.553
Although primarily
used in defense,

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:30.788
the sharp spikes, along
with the spike bud cap

00:21:30.888 --> 00:21:34.225
made it a menacing and
brutal weapon when in combat.

00:21:34.325 --> 00:21:36.695
Today, the sodegarami's
devastating use

00:21:36.761 --> 00:21:40.498
can be seen in the HBO
television series "Westworld."

00:21:40.565 --> 00:21:41.466
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:21:41.533 --> 00:21:44.403
Welcome to the kill test.

00:21:44.503 --> 00:21:47.539
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your sodegarami will do,

00:21:47.639 --> 00:21:49.307
I will take your
weapons and stab

00:21:49.374 --> 00:21:51.876
and try to snag this
ballistics dummy.

00:21:51.943 --> 00:21:52.711
 Rita, you're up first.

00:21:52.778 --> 00:21:53.411
You ready for this?

00:21:53.478 --> 00:21:54.613
- Hai.
- All right.

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:55.514
Let's do this.

00:22:00.285 --> 00:22:03.855
[rock music playing]

00:22:28.212 --> 00:22:29.213
 All right.

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:31.282
Let's talk about
your sodegarami.

00:22:31.349 --> 00:22:33.685
The tines you have
here penetrates.

00:22:33.752 --> 00:22:36.888
The hook you have here
will rip this person apart,

00:22:36.955 --> 00:22:40.359
and more importantly,
your weapon will kill.

00:22:42.527 --> 00:22:43.461
All right, Justin.
Your turn.

00:22:43.528 --> 00:22:44.262
You ready to have fun?

00:22:44.329 --> 00:22:45.030
 Yes, sir.

00:22:49.034 --> 00:22:52.604
[rock music playing]

00:23:10.922 --> 00:23:11.990
 All right, Justin.

00:23:12.090 --> 00:23:15.359
The tines you have here,
it's more of a stabbing tine

00:23:15.426 --> 00:23:16.561
rather than a grabbing.

00:23:16.628 --> 00:23:17.695
This is a grabbing weapon.

00:23:17.796 --> 00:23:20.431
But that hook does
grab onto that.

00:23:20.498 --> 00:23:22.334
Overall, sir, your weapon?

00:23:22.434 --> 00:23:23.402
Will kill.

00:23:28.406 --> 00:23:29.374
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:23:29.440 --> 00:23:30.942
It's time for the strength test.

00:23:31.009 --> 00:23:34.012
The dreaded ice block chop.

00:23:34.112 --> 00:23:36.281
Remember, this is not
about what these weapons do

00:23:36.347 --> 00:23:38.182
to the ice blocks,
but what those ice

00:23:38.249 --> 00:23:40.018
blocks do to your weapons.

00:23:40.118 --> 00:23:41.452
And Rita, you're up first.

00:23:41.519 --> 00:23:42.854
You get points for theme.

00:23:42.954 --> 00:23:47.592
I mean-- You ready?

00:23:47.659 --> 00:23:48.993
It doesn't matter, right?

00:23:49.060 --> 00:23:50.162
 No, it doesn't matter.

00:24:00.505 --> 00:24:03.708
[rock music playing]

00:24:25.029 --> 00:24:26.097
 All right, Rita.

00:24:26.164 --> 00:24:29.134
Got a little bit more of
a bend in this one tine

00:24:29.234 --> 00:24:31.736
here, but everything
else is pretty

00:24:31.836 --> 00:24:34.072
much the way it was going in.

00:24:34.172 --> 00:24:34.839
Definitely held up.

00:24:34.939 --> 00:24:35.440
Did its job.

00:24:35.540 --> 00:24:36.240
Good job.

00:24:36.340 --> 00:24:37.508
 Thank you.

00:24:37.575 --> 00:24:38.743
 All right, Justin.
Your turn.

00:24:38.843 --> 00:24:39.310
You ready?

00:24:39.410 --> 00:24:40.245
 Yes I am.

00:24:47.218 --> 00:24:50.155
[intense music playing]

00:25:08.873 --> 00:25:10.941
 All right, so you
survived the strength test.

00:25:11.042 --> 00:25:14.279
This is a very strong,
well-built head for this,

00:25:14.379 --> 00:25:18.616
but it's built more like a
spear than it is for catching.

00:25:18.682 --> 00:25:20.585
I mean, I'm not sure
how effective it would

00:25:20.685 --> 00:25:24.288
be at snagging the opponent,
but to devastate her,

00:25:24.355 --> 00:25:25.423
it certainly did the job.

00:25:25.490 --> 00:25:26.258
Good job.

00:25:30.595 --> 00:25:33.231
 All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the sharpness test,

00:25:33.297 --> 00:25:36.667
the Sandman Pierce and Capture.

00:25:36.734 --> 00:25:38.903
To test the sharpness,
I will take your weapon,

00:25:38.969 --> 00:25:41.605
pierce, and tried to
control this sandman.

00:25:41.672 --> 00:25:42.473
Rita, you're up first.

00:25:42.540 --> 00:25:43.207
You ready for this?

00:25:43.307 --> 00:25:44.075
 Yeah.

00:25:53.018 --> 00:25:56.555
[rock music playing]

00:26:15.073 --> 00:26:16.107
 All right Rita.

00:26:16.174 --> 00:26:17.642
The points you have
on your tines here

00:26:17.709 --> 00:26:20.078
definitely penetrate when
you thrust into that,

00:26:20.144 --> 00:26:22.513
but doesn't slice on
the way out or capture

00:26:22.613 --> 00:26:24.282
as well as it should.

00:26:24.348 --> 00:26:26.551
Your hook over here did its job.

00:26:26.651 --> 00:26:29.720
Overall, it will
cut and control.

00:26:29.787 --> 00:26:30.989
All right, Justin.
Your turn.

00:26:31.056 --> 00:26:31.489
So you ready?

00:26:31.556 --> 00:26:32.724
 Yes I am.

00:26:39.064 --> 00:26:42.601
[rock music playing]

00:26:53.478 --> 00:26:54.279
 Oh.

00:26:56.748 --> 00:26:57.816
That's not good.

00:27:01.619 --> 00:27:03.021
 He pulled it
out of the socket.

00:27:05.623 --> 00:27:07.325
 Well, Justin,
we have a problem.

00:27:07.425 --> 00:27:08.292
 Yes, sir.

00:27:08.359 --> 00:27:09.427
 This wasn't pinned was it?

00:27:09.494 --> 00:27:10.794
 No.

00:27:10.895 --> 00:27:12.764
 The impact from all
these tests loosened it up,

00:27:12.864 --> 00:27:14.633
and of course it came off.

00:27:17.769 --> 00:27:20.872
Justin, you brought in a
beautifully crafted weapon,

00:27:20.939 --> 00:27:23.375
however you've suffered
a catastrophic failure

00:27:23.441 --> 00:27:24.876
in our final test.

00:27:24.976 --> 00:27:28.746
And unfortunately, you cannot
be our Forged in Fire champion.

00:27:28.813 --> 00:27:29.881
 Congratulations, Rita.

00:27:29.981 --> 00:27:30.481
 Thank you.

00:27:30.581 --> 00:27:31.849
 Awesome.

00:27:31.916 --> 00:27:33.785
 Coming on Forged in
Fire, I put my all into it.

00:27:33.851 --> 00:27:35.586
And I feel like I
made a good weapon

00:27:35.686 --> 00:27:37.321
but just came up
short on a little bit

00:27:37.388 --> 00:27:38.556
of the fit and finish.

00:27:38.623 --> 00:27:40.058
And other than that,
I'm happy with it.

00:27:42.827 --> 00:27:44.462
 Rita, congratulations.

00:27:44.529 --> 00:27:46.731
You are the Forged
in Fire champion

00:27:46.798 --> 00:27:50.334
and that is a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:27:50.435 --> 00:27:51.836
Congratulations.

00:27:51.903 --> 00:27:54.606
How do you feel right now?

00:27:54.706 --> 00:27:55.773
 I just--

00:27:55.840 --> 00:27:58.042
 Come on forward
and shake our hands.

00:27:58.109 --> 00:27:59.110
Good job.

00:27:59.210 --> 00:28:01.011
 It's been a very
positive and uplifting

00:28:01.078 --> 00:28:04.181
experience to be able to do
something amazing like this.

00:28:04.281 --> 00:28:07.885
I hope this will help me
become an inspiration to kids

00:28:07.985 --> 00:28:10.555
because I can say, look,
if you see something

00:28:10.655 --> 00:28:12.823
and you want to try
it, give it a try.

00:28:12.890 --> 00:28:15.160
Hey, Weeblos, your scout
leader is the new Forged

00:28:15.226 --> 00:28:16.094
in Fire champion.

00:28:16.194 --> 00:28:17.495
I'm bringing it home.

00:28:17.562 --> 00:28:18.863
Can I have a group hug?

00:28:18.930 --> 00:28:19.764
Please?

00:28:19.831 --> 00:28:21.065
Thank you guys.

00:28:21.132 --> 00:28:21.933
Oh my God.

00:28:24.702 --> 00:28:27.972
[rock music playing]

